# Exact parachute-core source used by Cloud's shared @openparachute/core engine
# file dependency (workers/vault -> file:../../../parachute-core/packages/vault/core).
# CI and local deploys verify this commit so unrelated upstream work or a
# developer branch cannot change a build or deployment (cloud#45, cloud#59).
#
# The engine moved from parachute-vault (core/) into parachute-core
# (packages/vault/core/) with its history, via git subtree at vault 42fbf93
# (vault 0.7.9), which contains vault 1a66150 (#762). The previous pin, vault
# f147e34 (vault#785, T-36), was one commit on 1a66150; core#23 carries it over.
# Pinned at parachute-core main 86cbddd: a9c9024 (the T-36 fix production ran
# from vault#785, and T-318's import fix) plus the T-318 day review's engine
# fixes: path_prefix / exclude_path_prefix / rename-tag without LIKE under the
# Durable Object 50-byte LIKE cap (#27), one json_each param for a tag query
# over 100+ child tags under the 100-param cap (#28), a rename's cascade writes
# fire `updated` (#29), and restoring a snapshot the old exporter wrote keeps
# flow-looking metadata exact (#32). #30/#31 are CLI/hub only. The
# door-contract tree is untouched.
# Now pinned at parachute-core main 638c04a (#35, T-318 #8): a portable-md export
# that copies a note's attachment writes that note's `](/api/storage/<path>)`
# links to it as the relative path to `.parachute/attachments/<id>/<basename>`
# and records it as the ref's `body_link`; import turns back exactly those, so
# the body round-trips. The binaries are now written before their note, so in
# the /api/export tar an attachment entry precedes its note. Also between
# 86cbddd and here: 0.8.0-pre.2 (#33; in the engine only test fixture and
# comment wording) and docs (#34). packages/vault/src history-import and the
# CLI/hub changes are outside the engine Cloud builds.
# Now pinned at parachute-core main 8149a9e (#41, T-318 #16): a portable-md export
# names a pathless markdown note's file after its display title
# (`_unpathed/<title>.md`, safe characters, " 2"/" 3" for repeats compared without
# case) instead of `_unpathed/<id>.md`; import still reads id and path from the
# frontmatter, so old and new exports round-trip the same. computeDisplayTitle
# moved to core/src/display-title.ts so the exporter stays free of bun:sqlite.
# Also between 638c04a and here: docs/PRISM.md (#40), outside the engine.
# Now pinned at parachute-core uni/t412-scan-wake-forget (T-412, core PR to next; that branch is next plus
# T-395 #47 plus T-412): a Durable Object wake on a vault already at this schema runs no migration (it read the
# vault several times and wrote one index row per note, twice: v5 rebuilt a path index for v18 to drop); v5 no
# longer renames a note whose path differs from another's only by extension or case on every open; a
# case-insensitive path index (idx_notes_path_nocase, no SCHEMA_VERSION bump, so a rollback still opens the vault)
# makes path lookups indexed; a tag filter beside an indexed equality probes instead of listing the tag; delete can
# erase history (REST ?erase_history=true, MCP delete-note erase_history/ids, admin) and GET /history/deleted
# lists deleted notes with history left (erase takes only an exact id or case-sensitive path). Also T-395 (#47):
# bare metadata equality binds by type, list items with a colon round-trip, MCP query-notes since.
# Rollback to 8149a9e: the vault still opens (SCHEMA_VERSION unchanged; the extra index is harmless), but every wake
# runs every migration again, and v5's per-wake rename of a note whose path differs from another's only by extension
# or case comes back. A vault may already hold such `<path>-1` renames from before this pin.
# Now pinned at parachute-core uni/t421-batch-atomic (T-421, core PR to next; that branch is next f34b083 plus three
# engine commits): core's async batch seam (transactionAsync) uses the backend's own async transaction when it has
# one, and cloud's shim gives it ctx.storage.transaction, so a REST or MCP batch that fails part-way keeps nothing
# (audit L2-05; before, its BEGIN/COMMIT were shim no-ops and the first notes stayed). A blow-away import that passes
# `checkpoint` (cloud's) still commits in chunks, as before; and hooks (live pushes) fire only once a batch commits,
# so a rolled-back batch announces nothing. Rollback to f34b083: batches are non-atomic again.
# Now pinned at parachute-core next 419ca99, the squash of that branch (#58), so the pin is on next. Also in the
# engine between f34b083 and here: semantic search from a fresh install says when it can't (#50), import never
# follows a symlink out of its clone (#52), and an MCP tool crash leaves one server-log line (#57; cloud keeps its
# own workers/vault/src/error-log.ts). Rollback to f34b083 as above.
# Now pinned at parachute-core next 53f956f (T-421, core #59 squashed: the matcher moves into the engine): the live matcher is
# in the engine (core/src/live-match.ts) and cloud imports it instead of its copy, which compared bare filters
# loosely after #47 and delivered live what the query no longer found (audit L1-03). Rolling this pin back alone
# fails the build (the copy is deleted); roll back the whole PR.
#
# door/0.9 (T-430, the own-Cloudflare door; NOT next, which feeds Parachute Cloud): pinned at parachute-core next
# 64e2f40f, the 0.9.1 engine: #65 (the records REST door: /api/records, /api/types, ?type=), #68 (the write stamp: via
# names the key, by may name who it was for), #67 (tag-scope gaps closed on both REST doors), #74 (the read sentence,
# `connectionReach`). On top of 0.9.0 (#21) and 0.9.1's owner keys (#49): the record door, types as a tag kind (an
# additive `kind` column; no SCHEMA_VERSION bump an 0.8 engine can't open), the 0.9 vault projection, and the
# additive note_versions.via_kind column.
# door/0.9 cloud parity (T-456): pinned at parachute-core next 6c6b713, the squash of core #112 (the 0.9 tool surface, help, record
# words, typed refusals, the connect-time brief's scripting line, record HEAD and validators, and the REST name routes
# moved into the engine: core/src/mcp-surface.ts, http-validators.ts, name-routes.ts), on top of 0.9.2 and the 0.9.3
# merges up to #106 (#103 auto hybrid: off by default on cloud, CLOUD_HYBRID_AUTO_DEFAULT). The cloud door imports those instead of its own port (mcp-09.ts is gone). deploy-staging.sh takes
# this pin (Cloud staging runs the 0.9 door), and so does deploy-prod.sh (production deploys from door/0.9, Aaron 11-14). Rolling back means the whole
# door/0.9 PR: the engine modules it imports are not in 64e2f40f.
# door/0.9 for production (T-456, 11-14): pinned at parachute-core next bf453d8 (#125 on 909843f; its engine is 909843f's), which adds to 6c6b713: #100 (MCP
# annotations on every tool, from core mcp-annotations.ts; structuredContent where ChatGPT read a note by id as `{}`,
# core mcp-result.ts: both used by mcp.ts as a box uses them), #120 (meaning search reads each candidate's vectors by
# key), #124 (it scores each batch as it reads it, so memory doesn't grow with the vault), and the CLI's upgrade and
# rollback work (#119, #121, #122; outside the engine). Auto hybrid stays off by default here
# (CLOUD_HYBRID_AUTO_DEFAULT: still over its time gate on staging, mcp.ts). Rolling back to 6c6b713 alone fails the build (mcp.ts imports mcp-annotations.ts and
# mcp-result.ts): roll back the whole PR.
# door/0.9, T-476 (11-21): pinned at parachute-core next b1d2da5, which adds to bf453d8: #134 and #139 (write may define a
# type over MCP manage-types and over REST PUT /api/types/:name, and add fields to a type it made: core type-write.ts;
# tags gains created_by and created_via by ALTER, no SCHEMA_VERSION bump), #135 (a put-back is a change made now), and
# #140/#143 (core grants.ts, used by typed keys when this door takes them). The cloud door wires the type rule into
# its own router (vault-do.ts typeWriteOnly, rest/tags.ts) and passes MCP the writer's stamp (mcp.ts). Rollback to
# bf453d8: the vault opens (the new columns are ignored); a write key can no longer define types.
# door/0.9, T-476 (11-25): pinned at parachute-core 59c01658, the head of core PR #161 (branch uni/t476-one-refusal, on
# next 488a4dd; move this pin to its squash on next once #161 merges). It adds to b1d2da5 one way to refuse: every
# refusal of an MCP tools/call is an isError result with structuredContent {error_type, message, ...fields}, never a
# JSON-RPC error (core/src/mcp-refusal.ts: refusalOfError, refusalResult, unknownToolRefusal, internalRefusal); an
# in-band `{error, error_type}` reply is answered as one too (mcp-result.ts). Cloud's vault door imports the mapping
# instead of its copy (mcp.ts mapDomainError is gone) and the identity worker's account door imports the shape. Also in
# the engine: delete-tag's tag_referenced_as_parent has words. Rollback to b1d2da5 alone fails the build (mcp.ts and
# account-mcp-http.ts import mcp-refusal.ts): roll back the whole PR.
# Now pinned at parachute-core next a01c9980, the squash of #161 (11-25). Also in the engine between 59c01658 and here:
# add-attachment's inline store (#164, core/src/attachment/inline.ts; this door does not offer the tool yet), skills in a
# vault (#160: skills.ts; this door passes maySkills for an admin key that isn't typed, on MCP and REST, and answers a
# refused skill write with the box's 403 skill_needs_admin), the skill files and the connect-time "## Skills" section
# (#162: skill-files.ts, vault-projection.ts; the Skills extension itself is not served here yet), and record words a
# live page can trust (#159: `updatedAt` in update-record and the refusals). The REST blind-update words follow the box
# (refusal-hints.ts). Rollback: as above, the whole PR; a skill an admin wrote meanwhile stays a plain record.
# T-476 (11-27): pinned at parachute-core 4000df3, the head of core PR #173 (uni/t476-create-record-shapes; move to its
# squash on next once it merges). Production's health report showed create-record throwing TypeError for one vault;
# the engine now refuses every wrong argument shape before writing (core mcp.ts checkCreateShapes: a link needs a
# string target and relationship; path, body, created_at strings; tags an array of strings; records an array of
# objects), as invalid_query, where it crashed, often after writing the record. Also between a01c9980 and here: core
# #166's attachment words (add-attachment when the caller can't reach this host, as in claude.ai) and #168 (door
# contracts only). Rollback: the whole PR.
#
# The SHA is the entire pin. The engine package (packages/vault/core) is still
# 0.1.0 and never moves; PARACHUTE_CORE_VERSION is the workspace root version,
# checked so the pin's release line is legible, not as protection.
PARACHUTE_CORE_REPO_URL="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-core.git"
PARACHUTE_CORE_REF="4000df30eee5fc0a3434c8241847ad5d4f19ba48"
PARACHUTE_CORE_VERSION="0.9.0-pre.2"
CORE_ENGINE_DIR="packages/vault/core"
CORE_ENGINE_VERSION="0.1.0"
